   "type": "Motor Sampan Type Patrol Boat",
   "title": "Contact 9 · Motor Sampan Type Patrol Boat",
   "fields": {
    "type": "Motor Sampan Type Patrol Boat",
    "course": "Various",
    "speed": "Var.",
    "remarks": "About 150 ft. High bow. Two masts. Single stack. Showing lights when first sighted. Made battle surface. Expended 15 rds. of 4\" and 460 rds of 20 MM. Destroyed.",
    "narrative": "2130(I) Sighted light bearing 045°T. and rel. Changed course to close, and at 2134(I) Identified vessel as patrol boat with familiar box structure aft. SJ Radar picked up vessel at a range of 3400 yards. At 2136(I) Submerged. Closed target and continued ranging with SJ Radar. At 2143(I) With vessel about 1000 yards distant, bearing 330° rel., made battle surface. Opened fire with 4\" gun and 20 MM machine gun. The weather was clear, with no moon. The 4\" gun pointer reported that the light of the 20 MM tracers and explosions were blinding. Smoke frequently obscured the target after 4\" shell hits. No fire was observed. At"
   },
   "flags": [
    "Transcriber: Gun action; the only claim of the patrol.",
    "Narrative entry at 2143 I January 17, 1943 (page 6) describes this attack; its account is included here.",
    "Hand transcription, Fold3 image 268550847. The entry continues on report page 7, not transcribed. Comsubdiv 101 (Enclosure B, para. 4): 'The night battle surface, gun attack on the sampan patrol boat was very well conducted.'"
   ],
